quran[4]{c,v,t}:
  9,37,"Indeed, the number of months, according to Allah’s decree, is twelve months. It is (laid down) in Allah’s Book since the day He created the heavens and the earth. Out of them, four (Dhu al-Qa‘da, Dhu al-Hijja, Muharram and Rajab) are sacred. That is the upright calculation. So do not wrong yourself during these months (by getting involved in warfare). And fight all the (combatant) polytheists (in case they attack you) as they fight you all together. And know that Allah is with the God-conscious."
  9,38,"Indeed, postponing (the sacred months to continue fighting) is an increase in disbelief, by which the disbelievers are (further) led astray. They make it lawful one year, and forbid it another year, to reconcile (outwardly) with the number Allah has made inviolable. But in doing so, they permit what Allah has forbidden. Their evil deeds have been made fair-seeming to them. And Allah does not guide the disbelieving people."
  9,39,"O believers! What excuse do you have when it is said to you, ‘Go forth in the way of Allah’, and you sink heavily to the ground? Are you so pleased with the life of this world instead of the Hereafter? Yet the provision of the life of this world, compared with the Hereafter, is insignificant."
  9,40,"If you do not move forth, He will punish you with a painful torment and replace you with other people, and you will not harm Him in the least. And Allah is All-Capable of everything."
